>> title: Crispy Roast Potatoes
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: potato, roast, duck fat, sheet pan, side
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: crispy roast potatoes, roast potatoes, roasties, duck fat potatoes, crunchy potatoes, oven roasted potatoes
>> pairs-with: chimichurri, toum
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: parboil 8 min in alkaline water
>> step.2: drain and shake hard, then dry 5 min
>> step.3: heat the fat on the pan until it shimmers
>> step.4: roll in the hot fat, roast 425°F (220°C) 45 min
>> step.5: salt and scatter rosemary

Parboil @Yukon Gold potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; peeled, in 2-in chunks) in @water{3%qt}(2.8 L) with @kosher salt{2%Tbs} and @baking soda{1/2%tsp} ~simmer{8%min}, until the edge of a chunk crumbles against the side of the pan but the middle still holds. The baking soda is the trick and it is not optional: alkaline water breaks down the pectin on the outside of the potato and nothing else, which is what makes the next step possible.

Drain @&(~1)parboiled potatoes{} and shake them hard in the dry pan, lid on, four or five good rattles, until every surface is rough and pasty, then leave them ~dry{5%min} to steam off. You are trying to raise a layer of mashed potato on the outside of each chunk. That paste is what fries to glass in the oven; a smooth-sided potato has nothing to crisp.

Heat @duck fat{1/4%cup}(60 mL; or beef dripping, or a neutral oil) on a #sheet pan{} in the oven until it shimmers and moves like water when you tilt it.

Roll @&(~2)roughened potatoes{} in @&(~1)hot fat{} until each one is coated, space them out, and ~roast{45%min} at 425°F (220°C), turning them once at thirty minutes. Cold fat means the paste soaks it up and goes greasy; hot fat sets the outside on contact.

Scatter @flaky salt{1%tsp} and @rosemary{1%Tbs}(leaves only, chopped) over @&(~1)roast potatoes{} the moment they leave the oven. Rosemary put on at the start burns to a bitter needle in forty-five minutes.
